From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ios-blink-sideload <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:32:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS sideload: allow building Chrome without any app extension

ios/chrome/app/BUILD.gn sets _extension_toolchain unconditionally but only
uses it inside the ios_enable_*_extension blocks. The sideload args turn
all of those off (each extension would need its own App ID), and gn gen
then fails with "Assignment had no effect". Mark the variable as not
needed.

Status: verified at Chromium 4558926c (158.0.8127.0) on a Mac: without it
gn gen fails with args/simulator.gn, with it gn gen succeeds.

diff --git a/ios/chrome/app/BUILD.gn b/ios/chrome/app/BUILD.gn
index eac0593c15f744f2b013fdba87762d35ca62210e..eaefac00cace08078ad0469a96d09d51d16f4b92 100644
--- a/ios/chrome/app/BUILD.gn
+++ b/ios/chrome/app/BUILD.gn
@@ -1007,6 +1007,9 @@ chrome_app("chrome") {
 
 if (current_toolchain == default_toolchain && !ios_chrome_generate_order_file) {
   _extension_toolchain = "${current_toolchain}_app_ext"
+
+  # [ios-blink-sideload] Sideload builds turn off every extension below.
+  not_needed([ "_extension_toolchain" ])
   if (ios_enable_share_extension) {
     extension_bundle_data("share_extension_bundle") {
       extension_name = "share_extension.appex"
-- 
